Mint and revoke pairing credentials from the web client

The tile could not pair anything. "Generate code" for a phone did nothing, and
there was no way to hand another client access to this runtime at all.

Both surfaces are desktop-only IPC the web preload never had. This adds two
credential scopes over one mechanism: `mobile` offers for phones (RPC allowlist
plus payload diet) and `runtime` grants for full clients. Both mint or revoke a
credential, so both are authorized by the same `trustedMobilePairing` context,
injected only for runtime-scope connections and absent means fail closed. The
advertised address stays server policy (`--pairing-address`), never
client-chosen; strict zod params error rather than strip it.

To test, open Settings > Mobile in the tile, generate a code and pair a phone;
then generate a runtime share link and open it in another browser. Revoking
either should drop that client. Covered by `mobile-pairing.test.ts` and
`mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts`.

